      "description": "Bordered content surface with restrained card elevation.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-card\"><h2>Project activity</h2><p>Recorded errors and sessions appear here.</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-card{padding:16px;background:var(--card,#151a23);color:var(--foreground,#edf1f7);border:1px solid var(--border,#29313e);border-radius:8px;box-shadow:var(--shadow-card,0 1px 2px #0000000d);font-family:var(--font-sans,system-ui,sans-serif)}.ds-card h2{margin:0;font-size:14px;font-weight:650;line-height:1.4;letter-spacing:-.02em}.ds-card p{margin:4px 0 0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--muted-foreground,#929eaf)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Section tabs",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "tabs",
      "description": "Foreground active text and a primary underline identify the current section.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-tabs\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Preview sections\"><button role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">General</button><button role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">Members</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-tabs{display:flex;overflow-x:auto;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border,#29313e)}.ds-tabs button{padding:10px 12px;border:0;border-bottom:2px solid transparent;margin-bottom:-1px;background:transparent;color:var(--muted-foreground,#929eaf);font:500 14px var(--font-sans,system-ui,sans-serif);cursor:pointer;white-space:nowrap;transition:color 150ms,border-color 150ms}.ds-tabs button:hover{color:var(--foreground,#edf1f7)}.ds-tabs button[aria-selected=true]{color:var(--foreground,#edf1f7);border-bottom-color:var(--primary,#a5b4fc)}.ds-tabs button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--primary,#a5b4fc);outline-offset:3px}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-tabs button{transition-duration:.01ms}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Evidence disclosure",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "evidence-section",
      "description": "Native disclosure keeps recorded evidence grouped and keyboard accessible.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-evidence\"><details open><summary>Stack trace</summary><p>Recorded event frames appear here.</p></details><details><summary>Breadcrumbs</summary><p>Recorded messages and categories appear here.</p></details></div>",
      "css": ".ds-evidence{background:var(--card,#151a23);color:var(--foreground,#edf1f7);border:1px solid var(--border,#29313e);border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;font-family:var(--font-sans,system-ui,sans-serif)}.ds-evidence details+details{border-top:1px solid var(--border,#29313e)}.ds-evidence summary{display:flex;gap:8px;padding:12px;list-style:none;cursor:pointer;font-size:14px;font-weight:650;line-height:1.4;letter-spacing:-.02em}.ds-evidence summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}.ds-evidence summary::after{content:\"⌄\";margin-left:auto}.ds-evidence details:not([open]) summary::after{content:\"›\"}.ds-evidence summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--primary,#a5b4fc);outline-offset:-2px}.ds-evidence p{margin:0;padding:0 12px 12px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--muted-foreground,#929eaf)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Evidence-first developer triage",
    "overview": "replayd is a compact workbench for inspecting recorded errors and sessions. Cool neutral surfaces, indigo actions and explicit severity colors keep dense evidence readable. The owner-supplied compact design system replaces the former plum palette while retaining the familiar navigation, content hierarchy and interaction patterns.\n\nThe built source of truth is `dashboard/app/assets/css/main.css`, with Vue shared controls and the existing icon paths. Nuxt 4, Vue 3 and Tailwind 4 remain in place. System fonts and semantic tokens carry the same visual language through projects, triage, replay, settings, account and error screens.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Compact spacing and clear data hierarchy.",
      "Paired dark and light palettes with semantic severity.",
      "System sans text and monospace identifiers and measured values.",
      "Bordered surfaces with restrained elevation.",
      "Native controls, visible focus and reduced-motion support."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Paired Theme Rule",
        "body": "Change foreground, surface and border roles together. Primary action fill and white action text stay identical in both themes; links, focus and selection use the theme-specific primary color.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Measured Type Rule",
        "body": "Use monospace with tabular numerals for identifiers, code and aligned measurements. Keep interface prose in the system sans stack.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Bounded Surface Rule",
        "body": "Keep wide data and long technical strings inside their own scrolling or wrapping regions. Preserve table headings and reachable actions instead of shrinking values.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Quiet Depth Rule",
        "body": "Use thin borders to separate surfaces. Keep the small card shadow and reserve the larger shadow for surfaces that sit above the current task.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do reuse the central tokens and existing shared controls.",
      "Do inspect text, icons and their backgrounds together in both themes.",
      "Do preserve visible keyboard focus and test real pointer interactions.",
      "Do keep tables locally scrollable and technical identifiers readable.",
      "Do keep all displayed records, permissions and behaviors tied to the existing application."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't add fonts, UI libraries or a replacement component framework for styling.",
      "Don't hardcode a separate palette or font stack for an individual page.",
      "Don't change routes, copy, API calls or data handling to make a visual change.",
      "Don't increase virtualized row height with CSS alone; its geometry is controlled by existing code."
    ]
  }
}

